# The level tour (#596): every level of the game loaded on the simulated headset with loadlevel - 10 (the start),
# 0-8 and 11-23 (there is no level 9). Each level loads with no [E] line and no hang report, renders (frames in
# gameplay, a shot whose eyes got a picture) and logs one line with its frame time and the player's position:
#   [channel] levelstats: level 3 frames=244 mean=11.11 p95=12.18 max=12.88 player=7257.6 822.9 7663.8 exits=22 ladders=0
# The level's exits (the entities whose scripts change the level, with the zones they control) and ladders (the
# climbable polygons, grouped) go to <test dir>\level-tour.txt for later tasks (#479, #55).
# Manual (not in CI): the game runs about 2 minutes, 4-4.5 minutes with the launch and the checks - far over the
# 30 s a check of the merge gate may cost (docs/vr/TESTING.md "The level tour").
#   .\scripts\dev\xrs-run.ps1 manual\level-tour
# Every level is entered at a real entry marker - the target of an exit of another level (level-tour.txt) - as the
# game enters it. Without a target the player keeps the previous level's coordinates and often stands outside the
# new level (black eyes); that way level 21 crashed in its init once (#601), not at its real entry.
# A level that fails is a bug issue, and its failing step here an @pending #<issue> - never a weaker check.
# Frame rate is guaranteed in level 1 only (the owner, #596): the times are measured and logged, not judged. They
# read the PC's load too (two runs beside other games: 17-32 ms means on different levels each time), so compare runs
# made while no other game runs.
@sim idle
@solo
@args --loadlevel 10

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until hangWatchdog.watching eq true 30s

# --- Level 10: the start (--loadlevel 10)
@remember errors10 errors
@assert area eq 10
@nolog ^\[[EC]\]                                  # no error or critical line in the load
@nolog \[hang\] main thread stalled               # nor a hang report
@frames 30                                       # past the load's frame and its first texture uploads
levelstats start
@frames 240                                      # about 3 s at 90 Hz: also past the level's fade-in (TRAPS.md)
levelstats report
@log \[channel\] levelstats: level 10 frames=\d+ mean=[\d.]+ p95=[\d.]+ max=[\d.]+ player=\S+ \S+ \S+ exits=\d+ ladders=\d+
@assert state eq GAMEPLAY
@assert levelStats.frames ge 239
@shot level-10
@assert vr.sim.shots.level-10.left.scene.verdict ne background
@assert vr.sim.shots.level-10.right.scene.verdict ne background
@assert errors eq {errors10}

